<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Organizations on Layer5 Documentation</title><link>/pr-preview/pr-1337/cloud/guides/organizations/</link><description>Recent content in Organizations on Layer5 Documentation</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en</language><atom:link href="/pr-preview/pr-1337/cloud/guides/organizations/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>User Management</title><link>/pr-preview/pr-1337/cloud/guides/organizations/managing-users/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>/pr-preview/pr-1337/cloud/guides/organizations/managing-users/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;This guide outlines methods for creating user accounts, adding users to organizations, inviting new members, and managing user access within Layer5 Cloud to maintain a secure and organized environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;




&lt;div class="md__image"&gt;
 &lt;picture&gt;
 &lt;source srcset="/pr-preview/pr-1337/contentimg/cloud/guides/organizations/managing-users/images/org_invite_hu_8dc70b7353643a06.webp" type="image/webp" width="2260" height="982"&gt;
 &lt;img src="images/org_invite.png" onclick="openModal(this)" alt="User Management options"
 width="2260" height="982"
 class="md-image-responsive" /&gt;
 &lt;/picture&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2 id="create-user-account" class="heading-link"&gt;
 Create User Account
 &lt;a href="#create-user-account" class="heading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink to this heading"&gt;🔗&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Seamlessly initiate new user accounts, ensuring a smooth onboarding process. Specify user details, such as email, and tailor their access by adding them to one or more organizations. Optionally assign roles, defining their scope within the platform. Complete the process by sending a personalized account setup email, streamlining the user&amp;rsquo;s introduction to Layer5 Cloud.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>User Invitations</title><link>/pr-preview/pr-1337/cloud/guides/organizations/inviting-users/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>/pr-preview/pr-1337/cloud/guides/organizations/inviting-users/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;The &lt;a href="https://cloud.layer5.io/identity/invitations"&gt;invitation system&lt;/a&gt; gives you precise control over how members join your organization, allowing you to streamline onboarding and enhance security.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You can create highly customized invitations for any scenario, from onboarding specific individuals to launching large-scale community challenges. Each invitation can be configured with expiration dates, usage quotas, and pre-assigned roles, ensuring new members get the right access from the moment they join.&lt;/p&gt;






&lt;div class="alert alert-custom" style="border-color: #3772ff;" role="alert"&gt;
 &lt;h4 class="alert-heading" style="color: #3772ff;"&gt;Required permission&lt;/h4&gt;
 
 From Layer5 Cloud v1.0.293, creating, editing, and deleting invitations requires the &lt;strong&gt;Manage Invitations&lt;/strong&gt; permission within your organization. That one permission also covers choosing the roles and teams an invitation grants, so anyone who can write an invitation, Academy Admins included, can specify its roles. Contact your organization administrator if you need access.
 
&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h3 id="default-organization-state" class="heading-link"&gt;
 Default organization state
 &lt;a href="#default-organization-state" class="heading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink to this heading"&gt;🔗&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By default, organizations are &lt;strong&gt;closed&lt;/strong&gt;: there is no open registration. A user cannot join your organization simply by navigating to a URL - they must either click a valid invitation link or register through a page associated with an organization that has a &lt;a href="/pr-preview/pr-1337/cloud/guides/organizations/inviting-users/#invitation-properties-explained"&gt;default invitation&lt;/a&gt; configured.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Organization Configuration Scenarios</title><link>/pr-preview/pr-1337/cloud/guides/organizations/configuration-scenarios/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>/pr-preview/pr-1337/cloud/guides/organizations/configuration-scenarios/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Every organization in Layer5 Cloud is configured by two choices: &lt;strong&gt;where your users sign in&lt;/strong&gt; (the front door) and &lt;strong&gt;whose identity provider authenticates them&lt;/strong&gt;. The combinations form five named scenarios. This guide helps you pick one and then walks through the settings that implement it, including who is allowed to change each setting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For the mechanics behind the choices, see &lt;a href="/pr-preview/pr-1337/cloud/guides/self-hosted/white-labeling/"&gt;White-labeling&lt;/a&gt; (themes, logos, custom domains) and &lt;a href="/pr-preview/pr-1337/cloud/guides/self-hosted/planning/identity-services/"&gt;Identity Services&lt;/a&gt; (bring-your-own-credentials and authentication boundaries).&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Manage Teams</title><link>/pr-preview/pr-1337/cloud/guides/organizations/managing-teams/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>/pr-preview/pr-1337/cloud/guides/organizations/managing-teams/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;This guide covers the administrator tasks for teams. For what a team is and how it grants access, read the &lt;a href="/pr-preview/pr-1337/cloud/concepts/identity-and-security/teams/"&gt;Teams concept&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;














